content.text:
I feel you. The current setup still has a dual-update seam:

- Runtime behavior lives in ProcPackage scripts.
- Player-facing numbers live in summaries/display metadata.

That means a balance change can still require updating two places.

The better model is:

```js
ProcPackage {
  params: {
    healthCostPct: 0.08,
    fireDamage: 5,
  },
  display: {
    format: "Spend {healthCostPct}% max HP for +{fireDamage} fire damage.",
  },
  script: (ctx, params) => { ... }
}
```

The script and tooltip both consume the same canonical `params`. Items only reference the package. No per-item description maintenance, and no separate prose numbers to keep synchronized.

The work so far improves inheritance and visibility, but I would not mass-convert more packages until we make that parameter ownership change.

